cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "msfPDF: Sub-Millisecond Zero-Dependency %PDF-1.4 Vector Document Engine"
message: "If you use msfPDF in software, benchmarks, or research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Felisberto
    given-names: Murilo
    affiliation: "Edinburgh, Scotland, United Kingdom"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-03"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mfelisberto90/msfPDF"
url: "https://mfelisberto90.github.io/msfPDF/"
abstract: >-
  Clean-room, sub-millisecond (0.16-0.52 ms) ISO 32000-1 (%PDF-1.4) vector document compiler
  with 1:1 byte parity across Rust, zero-dependency Web-Standard TypeScript, and a standalone CLI.
  Provides WinAnsi 7-bit octal encoding, dynamic 2048-UPM Type 3 vector glyph subsetting for
  Russian/Slavic Cyrillic and connected Arabic RTL (with contextual shaping, Lam-Alef ligatures,
  UAX #9 BiDi reordering, and searchable /ToUnicode CMaps), pure GF(256) Reed-Solomon vector QR codes,
  integer minor-unit currency formatting, and atomic 0600 multi-tenant vault storage.
keywords:
  - pdf-generation
  - pdf-1.4
  - zero-dependency
  - rust
  - typescript
  - arabic-shaping
  - rtl
  - cyrillic
  - vector-qr-code
  - ssrf-prevention
  - fintech
  - multi-tenant-security
